Miriam was a wonderful experience and exactly the kind of neighborhood restaurant that makes New York feel special. Anne and I had such a lovely meal there on Seventh Avenue near my apartment, and from the moment we walked in, the energy was warm, welcoming, and genuinely inviting without ever feeling overwhelming.

The Mediterranean cuisine was excellent, the service was top-notch, and the whole evening had that rare balance of professionalism and comfort that makes you want to come back again and again. Raphael, the owner, was especially gracious — smiling, attentive, and checking in on guests in a way that made the restaurant feel personal and full of heart.

